From 5448e293f372db647a2f73eb7166b3004b38a1eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Slava P." <slavap@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:41:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] rdna-boosts [optional]: two-lane prefill
 (LLAMA_PREFILL_LANES) -- consecutive-ubatch overlap

The `two-lane-prefill` artifact, re-cut against the r259 release tree (commit c80fa8bda, tree
7995db440ff79d805b4e1ad946ebfae605a56616) from the r254 cut of PR #301 (which was the r246 cut of
PR #296 rebased), which carries the change requested in the PR #284 review (recorded in main as
39206ffe): the MTP *target* pairs, and the MTP *draft* is refused at the arm gate by `ctx_type`.
NOT part of the delivery: nothing here is in `patches/`, `release.json` or
`rdna-boosts-all.patch`, and only `scripts/apply-all.sh --include-optional` picks it up.  Applying it to
`release.json`'s tree produces tree d1c3f0f9c370efc7707caab10ebc6c67c03bfe9a.

What it does
------------
`LLAMA_PREFILL_LANES=2` keeps a second backend scheduler (its own compute buffers) and, in the
decode loop, prepares two consecutive wide prefill ubatches on the two lanes and submits their
splits alternately, so one device's routed-expert work overlaps another device's attention.
A batch of [LLAMA_LANES_SPLIT_MIN (default 1024; 0 disables), 2 x n_ubatch) tokens is split
into two wide sub-ubatches (LLAMA_LANES_SPLIT_FRAC, default 0.55, rounded up to 64 = the
chunked-GDN chunk) and the batch's output row lands in the second one; either partner may carry
outputs, extracted per lane on that lane's scheduler.  It degrades to the single-lane path with
< 2 non-CPU backends, pipeline parallelism, no_alloc, a draft context, or a workload that reads
F1 layer-input rows.  Requires a layout where pipeline parallelism is already off: `-sm layer`
plus any `--override-tensor`.

Re-cut delta versus the r254 cut (PR #301, patch sha bf6f8f39)
--------------------------------------------------------------
1. Base drift r254 -> r259.  Two delivery changes moved the base under the artifact: r258 (block 09:
   the identity expert table is served IN PLACE, no band restriction -- ggml-backend-impl.h gains
   `moe_cache_in_place`, ggml-backend.cpp's staging decision and take-over call change, and
   `ggml_backend_buffer_get_usage()` answers for a buffer-less table) and r259 (block 01: the
   copy-engine all-reduce's `q8ce` wire, ggml-cuda.cu).  Code delta: none.  The artifact's +/-
   line set is identical across the r247, r254 and r259 cuts (checked per file, `sort`ed line
   multisets): the arm gate, MTP-target pairing, draft refusal and the scheduler refactor are
   unchanged.
2. The r254 cut's own delta note had the attribution wrong: `GGML_SCHED_STAGE_MODE` was retired by
   **r250** (block 09, `TODO` #284 -- the redirect's benefit was one D2D, +0.2-0.3 %), not by r254
   and not by blocks 12-15.  Corrected here; the resolution itself (take the two-lane per-split
   refactor, do not reintroduce the retired redirect block) was right.
3. FIXED: `LLAMA_PREFILL_LANES=2` aborted at the first prefill on a host-expert layout
   (`-sm layer -ot ... -ncmoe N`): `GGML_ASSERT(sched_a->is_alloc && sched_b->is_alloc)` in
   `ggml_backend_sched_graph_compute_async_pair`.  `prepare_ubatch()` gained the `lane` parameter in
   this artifact, but the delivery's two lane-0 placement blocks inside it -- the ring narrow->wide
   drop (`ring_carved && ring_arm && n_tokens_prev < 64`) and the `drop_now` wide->narrow
   drop/re-reserve -- still dropped and re-reserved `sched` (lane 0) unconditionally, so the lane-1
   prepare ran them AGAIN after lane 0's ubatch was prepared and left lane 0 unallocated for the
   pair.  Both blocks are now `lane == 0` (they manipulate lane 0's scheduler and the context's
   lane-0 size expectations; a lane-1 ubatch must not re-place lane 0).  Pre-existing since the
   r246 cut -- it was never seen because the artifact's arms all keep the experts device-resident.
   Verified: the arm now runs, text identical to the single-lane arm (`e2dde701fc04`, 35B-A3B
   Q8_0, 3 x R9700).
4. Dropped a stray blank line the artifact had been adding to `ggml/include/ggml-cuda.h` since the
   r220 cut (it was that file's only change there); the file is untouched now.

Measured on this cut (3 x R9700 / gfx1201, `-sm layer -ts 1/1/1 -ot blk\.0\.attn_q\.weight=ROCm0`,
the only layout the pair reaches): default path bit-identical (prefill-logit gate mean KLD
0.000000 / same-top-p 100.000 %); 35B-A3B Q8_0 `llama-bench pp2048 -b 2048 -ub 2048`
6534.7 -> 8063.1 t/s (+23.4 %); dense 27B MTP target prefill +29.2 %, dense `--spec-type none`
+22.3 %, greedy text unchanged in every arm; and on host-resident experts (`-ncmoe 40`) it is
+5.6 % at the default `-ub 512` and **-11.8 %** at `-ub 2048`, so that tier should leave the knob
off.  Full tables, the reachability matrix and the open points are in
`optional/two-lane-prefill/README.md`.
